1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,162
Magnesium ribbon is added to dilute hydrochloric acid in one tube, and marble chips, calcium carbonate,

2
00:00:06,162 --> 00:00:11,909
to the acid in another. Both fizz. Predict: is the same gas made in both tubes? Pause and decide.

3
00:00:12,969 --> 00:00:18,183
Watch. A lit splint held at the mouth of the magnesium tube goes out with a squeaky pop.

4
00:00:19,242 --> 00:00:23,863
The gas from the marble chips is bubbled through limewater, which turns milky.

5
00:00:24,923 --> 00:00:27,707
Explain what you saw. The gases are different.

6
00:00:27,707 --> 00:00:32,211
Acid plus metal gives a salt plus hydrogen, which burns with a squeaky pop.

7
00:00:32,211 --> 00:00:37,958
Acid plus a metal carbonate gives a salt, water and carbon dioxide, which turns limewater milky.

8
00:00:37,958 --> 00:00:44,120
Both tubes make a salt: magnesium chloride and calcium chloride. Pause and explain it in your own words.

9
00:00:45,179 --> 00:00:47,905
Salts can also be made from metal carbonates.

10
00:00:47,905 --> 00:00:52,171
Drop a seashell, made of calcium carbonate, into vinegar and it fizzes.

11
00:00:52,171 --> 00:00:55,963
Acid plus metal carbonate gives salt, carbon dioxide and water.

12
00:00:55,963 --> 00:00:59,222
Sulfuric acid and copper carbonate make copper sulfate.

13
00:01:00,281 --> 00:01:06,621
Acid plus metal gives salt plus hydrogen: hydrochloric acid and zinc make zinc chloride. We use magnesium,

14
00:01:06,621 --> 00:01:12,546
iron or zinc, because copper, silver and gold don't react, and sodium and potassium are too violent.

15
00:01:13,605 --> 00:01:19,945
To prepare copper sulfate, warm dilute sulfuric acid gently, then add copper carbonate a little at a time,

16
00:01:19,945 --> 00:01:26,166
stirring, until some is left over and no longer reacts. Adding excess makes sure all the acid is used up.

17
00:01:27,225 --> 00:01:32,439
Filter the mixture to remove the unreacted copper carbonate. Collect the blue filtrate,

18
00:01:32,439 --> 00:01:38,364
then heat it gently in an evaporating dish to remove most of the water, making a saturated solution.

19
00:01:39,424 --> 00:01:43,986
Leave the saturated solution to cool, and blue copper sulfate crystals form.

20
00:01:43,986 --> 00:01:46,474
Filter them and dry them on filter paper.

21
00:01:46,474 --> 00:01:50,503
The same method makes zinc chloride from zinc and hydrochloric acid.

22
00:01:51,563 --> 00:01:57,073
Now it is your turn to shine! Pause the video after each question and try to answer it first.

23
00:01:58,132 --> 00:02:02,043
Question 1: Complete: acid plus base gives... Pause the video now.

24
00:02:03,102 --> 00:02:04,465
Answer: Salt and water.

25
00:02:05,524 --> 00:02:11,390
Question 2: Which gas is given off when an acid reacts with a metal carbonate? Pause the video now.

26
00:02:12,449 --> 00:02:13,812
Answer: Carbon dioxide.

27
00:02:14,871 --> 00:02:19,907
Question 3: Name the salt made from sulfuric acid and magnesium. Pause the video now.

28
00:02:20,967 --> 00:02:22,507
Answer: Magnesium sulfate.

29
00:02:23,566 --> 00:02:28,780
Question 4: Why is excess metal carbonate added when making a salt? Pause the video now.

30
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:32,269
Answer: To make sure all the acid reacts.
